# Named args are never type-discriminated into typed buckets — they always go to rest.
# The ...ns@Int bucket gets positional Int args; the rest bucket gets the named arg.
# This verifies the caller-intent invariant: named args are not routed by type.
[call [fn [let]
  [f: [fn [let ...ns@Int ...rest] [builtin-dict-length rest]]]
  [f 1 2 3 extra: "hello"]]]
=== out
Int(1)
